# quiet
# diskwait.lic  (first line `# quiet`: Lich skips its "active"/"has exited" lines, so a
# run where the disk is already here prints nothing in the game window)
#
# Run in a prerest right before ;eloot sell. Waits up to MAX_WAIT seconds for your
# floating disk to catch up and show in the room, so eloot sees it.
#
# Why: 10/28, 02:29. go2/eherbs walk faster than the disk follows, so Fizzlestiks
# reached the inn and ;eloot sell started a second or two before "Your disk arrives,
# following you dutifully." eloot 2.14.1 seeds its disk from Disk.mine once, when the
# sell starts, and its wait_for_disk returns straight away when that's nil. So it
# never looked on the disk, took no boxes to the locksmith pool, and at the pawnshop
# (by then the disk had caught up) it stored the two closed boxes it found there in
# the velvet cloak and the snowcat haversack ("** fluted steel coffer is closed.
# Storing box..."). That filled both, and at 03:06 eloot paused holding a blue crystal
# it had nowhere to put (see eloot_guard.lic).
#
#   ;diskwait     wait for the disk, then exit (right away if it's already here)

module Diskwait

MAX_WAIT = 10 unless defined?(MAX_WAIT) # seconds; on 10/28 it lagged 2-3 s behind go2

def self.disk_here?
  !Disk.mine.nil?
rescue StandardError
  false
end

unless disk_here?
  (MAX_WAIT * 5).times do
    break if disk_here?

    sleep 0.2
  end
  echo "diskwait: no disk in the room after #{MAX_WAIT} s, so eloot will sell without it." unless disk_here?
end

end # module
